      "content": "<strong>अध्याय 9: सामान्य अंग्रेज़ी</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vh2ho6g",
      "content": "<em>Grammar, Vocabulary &amp; Comprehension for Paper 1</em>"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "tvqhjnx",
      "content": "<strong>  9.1 Parts of Speech</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "33toe22",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Part of Speech</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Definition</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Example</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Noun</p>",
            "<p>Name of person/place/thing</p>",
            "<p>Ram, Delhi, book, beauty</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Pronoun</p>",
            "<p>Used in place of noun</p>",
            "<p>I, he, she, they, it</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Adjective</p>",
            "<p>Modifies noun/pronoun</p>",
            "<p>tall, beautiful, three</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Verb</p>",
            "<p>Action or state of being</p>",
            "<p>run, sing, is, was</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Adverb</p>",
            "<p>Modifies verb/adjective/adverb</p>",
            "<p>quickly, very, here, often</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Preposition</p>",
            "<p>Shows relation between words</p>",
            "<p>in, on, at, by, with, for</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Conjunction</p>",
            "<p>Joins words or clauses</p>",
            "<p>and, but, or, because, if</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Interjection</p>",
            "<p>Exclamation</p>",
            "<p>Oh! Ah! Wow! Alas!</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "9y36xk2",
      "content": "<strong>  9.2 Tenses — Quick Reference</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "59ar718",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Tense</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Structure</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Example</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Simple Present</p>",
            "<p>S + V1(s/es) + O</p>",
            "<p>He writes a letter.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Present Continuous</p>",
            "<p>S + is/am/are + V-ing + O</p>",
            "<p>He is writing a letter.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Present Perfect</p>",
            "<p>S + has/have + V3 + O</p>",
            "<p>He has written a letter.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Present Perfect Continuous</p>",
            "<p>S + has/have been + V-ing + O</p>",
            "<p>He has been writing for 2 hours.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Simple Past</p>",
            "<p>S + V2 + O</p>",
            "<p>He wrote a letter.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Past Continuous</p>",
            "<p>S + was/were + V-ing + O</p>",
            "<p>He was writing a letter.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Past Perfect</p>",
            "<p>S + had + V3 + O</p>",
            "<p>He had written the letter.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Past Perfect Continuous</p>",
            "<p>S + had been + V-ing + O</p>",
            "<p>He had been writing for 2 hours.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Simple Future</p>",
            "<p>S + will + V1 + O</p>",
            "<p>He will write a letter.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Future Continuous</p>",
            "<p>S + will be + V-ing + O</p>",
            "<p>He will be writing a letter.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Future Perfect</p>",
            "<p>S + will have + V3 + O</p>",
            "<p>He will have written.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Future Perfect Continuous</p>",
            "<p>S + will have been + V-ing + O</p>",
            "<p>He will have been writing.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "n697ese",
      "content": "<strong>  9.3 Active &amp; Passive Voice</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "g5a42ca",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Active Voice</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Passive Voice</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Ram writes a letter.</p>",
            "<p>A letter is written by Ram.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>She is singing a song.</p>",
            "<p>A song is being sung by her.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>They have completed the work.</p>",
            "<p>The work has been completed by them.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>The manager approved the plan.</p>",
            "<p>The plan was approved by the manager.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>He will finish the project.</p>",
            "<p>The project will be finished by him.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xnutg6b",
      "content": "<strong>  9.4 Reported Speech</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "37dcjsg",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Direct Speech</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Indirect Speech</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>He said, \"I am happy.\"</p>",
            "<p>He said that he was happy.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>She said, \"I will come tomorrow.\"</p>",
            "<p>She said that she would come the next day.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>He said, \"I went there yesterday.\"</p>",
            "<p>He said that he had gone there the day before.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>He said to me, \"Are you well?\"</p>",
            "<p>He asked me if I was well.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>She said, \"Please help me.\"</p>",
            "<p>She requested me to help her.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "wh70vbr",
      "content": "<strong>  9.5 Common Errors (Error Spotting)</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "rg49su5",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Incorrect</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Correct</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>He is more better than me.</p>",
            "<p>He is better than me. (No double comparative)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Each of the students have passed.</p>",
            "<p>Each of the students has passed. (Each = singular)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Neither of them were present.</p>",
            "<p>Neither of them was present. (Neither = singular)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>She is one of the best student.</p>",
            "<p>She is one of the best students. (best + plural)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>He told that he was ill.</p>",
            "<p>He said that he was ill. (told needs object)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>I have seen him yesterday.</p>",
            "<p>I saw him yesterday. (yesterday = simple past)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>She is junior than me.</p>",
            "<p>She is junior to me. (junior/senior + to)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
